      "type": "原文",
      "type_label": "原文",
      "text": "The Maxwell spacecraft is in orbit and ready to get to work. \n\nThe spacecraft we built for @viasat launched from Cape Canaveral yesterday. \n\nOver the next five months, it will demonstrate how Viasat's ViaSat-3 Ka-band and global L-band networks can give low Earth orbit missions near real-time data and telemetry, tracking and command (TT&C) at any point in orbit, supporting @NASA's Communications Services Project as it prepares to retire its TDRS fleet.\n\nCongratulations to the Viasat team on a successful launch!",
